                                        "entry_id": "8fd4acff-b9fc-3a61-aa5b-898577c00cbf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of puer (“dung (e.g. of dogs)”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aadf0a83-7105-44bb-9e47-f3b20da9b72f",
                                                "sense_id": "be19f5bd-f9fe-3fae-b1df-0cd1319d08a2",
                                                "text": "[…] Dogs'-dung is called ‘Pure’, from its cleansing and purifying properties."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94baba91-5b48-4dfa-ba9e-eb5a4cb7ee49",
                                                "sense_id": "be19f5bd-f9fe-3fae-b1df-0cd1319d08a2",
                                                "text": "Mary smelled the rancid odor of the tannery on the right side of the road.[…]\n\"What is that, Mary?\" Jake asked.\n\"'Tis a bag for collecting pure. That is going to be your job, Jake. You are to collect pure.\"\n\"Pure? What is pure?\"\n\"Pure is another word for dung,\" Mary answered."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f7ee794-a7f5-4e21-9cf4-ebeb8d7b73f7",
                                                "sense_id": "be19f5bd-f9fe-3fae-b1df-0cd1319d08a2",
                                                "text": "[…] surely there was something better for him than chasing the pure (footnote: A term, technically speaking, for dog muck, much prized by the tanneries.) […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
